1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:13,070
Welcome to Update 22 of AHEAD Pathway. Your monthly check-in becomes a conversation: the Director replies, you respond, and you keep track of your own commitments.

2
00:00:14,470 --> 00:00:38,500
Every month, the Director reads your check-in and replies to you personally, here on your Check-in page, and you are notified. His reply speaks to what you actually did. You can respond once, right there, with no emails back and forth. Specific feedback on your own work builds confidence, and a sense that your progress is in your hands.

3
00:00:39,899 --> 00:01:01,199
Each month you also make one commitment: what will you do before your next check-in? Next month you say how it went: I did it, Partly, or Not this time, and what helped or got in the way. A commitment you name yourself, and look back on a month later, turns a report into a habit of progress.

4
00:01:02,599 --> 00:01:15,269
Your commitment also appears in Decisions and actions. And anything the Director promises in his reply becomes his action there, such as comments returned within ten working days.

5
00:01:16,669 --> 00:01:31,969
The Director may also share what the whole group told him, and what he is doing about it, with no names. And at the foot of the page, My check-in record gives you every month, with his replies, in one Word document.

6
00:01:33,369 --> 00:01:48,679
On his side, the Director answers each person in turn. He sees what you wrote, and a count of your month on Pathway, writes his reply, and lists what he will do. Each line becomes his action.

7
00:01:50,079 --> 00:02:13,219
October's check-in opens on the 24th of October: about ten minutes, seen by the Director only. Say how your commitment went, name the next one, and watch for his reply. Your check-in is now a conversation, not a form. That is AHEAD Pathway: your degree, well supported, every step of the way.
